    "statement": "On the guarded positive 433-1b cell-9 common curve, the necessary first-pair cuts for omitted DE and -DE records are respectively P(m,-m)=0 and P(-m,-m)=0, where m=B(-t^2)/A(-t^2). Exact four-basis norms on the complete six-chart cover have chart-invariant deployed root sets: 11 roots per source-sign positive row and 13 per negative row. Direct replay of all norm and inverse candidates leaves four ordinary positive-cut points and two ordinary negative-cut points per source-sign row. It also finds exactly two A=B=0 points per row, and these are precisely the previously regularized section-base points. There is no unresolved source branch. No target residual or outside-label exclusion is claimed.",
